  "purpose": "Non-regression evidence for a deliberate core change to the actor policy, and the direct test of whether that change removes the CP5-B false-pass finding.",
  "core_change": {
    "files": [
      "jev_ultrafast/questions.py",
      "jev_ultrafast/agent.py"
    ],
    "what": "NEXT_ACTION previously asserted that recent WAIT actions are not evidence of loading, with no rule licensing continued waiting. The actor therefore abandoned journeys while a submitted operation was still running and its in-progress text was on screen. The policy now licenses waiting while an operation is visibly running, and the bound on that loop moved from prompt wording into code as MAX_UNCHANGED_WAITS.",
    "why": "CP5-B reported 7 of 60 journeys passing while the browser actor had silently abandoned them. All 7 had visible in-progress text, so this was an actor defect, not a fixture artifact and not a Jev misclassification."
  },
